From dfc6bb3b6db55839a5b69399cdd0cd1d48b7b5d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 20:17:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sdk_fman: restore IRQs on sysfs handler early returns

Nineteen show handlers in the FMan sysfs wrappers take local_irq_save()
and then return directly from a validity check inside the critical
section -- device not active, no PCD handle, no params page, or a failed
sscanf of the attribute name -- leaving hardirqs disabled on the calling
CPU for the rest of that task's lifetime.

The attributes are all S_IRUGO, so any unprivileged read of an inactive
port or an unconfigured PCD trips this. Once it fires, the return path
back through seq_read_iter() -> copy_to_user() faults with hardirqs off
and splats might_fault(), and every subsequent scheduling decision on
that CPU runs with interrupts disabled.

Hoist each check -- and the sscanf that parses the attribute index --
above local_irq_save(), matching the idiom show_fm_risc_load() already
uses. Nothing being checked is derived inside the critical section, so
the ordering change is safe; only the register dumps that actually need
the guarantee stay under it.

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
